From 616de865539c5cf73d1e4688fc9ab74754710366 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor <victor@local>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 08:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] tp: 0019a CUDA-event phase profiler for the dist forward path

Adds `SPARKINFER_K3_DIST_PROFILE=1`: per-phase CUDA-event timings for the
distributed decode step, broken out as embed / attn / attn_ar / ffn_partial /
moe_ar / ffn_finish / head / sync_d2h, each with a percentage of the step.

Sampling is deliberately not "every token". Load and the first forwards are
wildly unrepresentative (allocator warmup, NCCL channel setup, first-touch page
faults), so the profiler skips a warmup window and then samples a bounded
number of steady tokens:

    SPARKINFER_K3_DIST_PROFILE_SKIP=N    warm tokens skipped   (default 8)
    SPARKINFER_K3_DIST_PROFILE_EVERY=N   sample every Nth      (default 1)
    SPARKINFER_K3_DIST_PROFILE_MAX=N     stop after N samples  (default 16)

The all-reduce buckets also carry their element counts (`n=`), because on this
engine collective cost tracks payload size and a millisecond number without the
count is not interpretable.

Mechanism: phases are wrapped in `DistProf::timed()`, which records a CUDA event
either side of the phase and accumulates the elapsed time. This is why the
direct `embed_token(...)` call becomes a `run_embed` lambda -- `timed()` needs
the phase as a callable so the same call site can be used with or without
instrumentation. When profiling is off, `timed()` sees a null event handle and
degrades to a plain `fn()` call, so the profile-off path is the original code
with no events, no syncs and no added work.

Note that `timed()` calls `cudaEventSynchronize` per phase, so an ACTIVE profile
run serializes the step and its absolute tok/s is not a valid benchmark number.
The percentages are the output to read, not the totals.

This is the instrumentation the TP3 decode-time breakdown came from (attention
~36.5%, collectives ~26.2%, MoE ffn_partial ~23.5%), which is what established
that this engine is bandwidth-bound and pointed the speed campaign at
speculative decoding rather than more kernel tuning.

Provenance: like the multi-prompt feature captured as 0015, this was written and
used on the fleet but never captured as a numbered patch. Patch 0020 was diffed
against a tree that already had it, so 0020 carries `run_embed` as an unchanged
*context* line and cannot apply to a clean 0001-0019 checkout without this.
Numbered 0019a rather than renumbering the series, since 0020+ are already
referenced by number in APPLY.md and elsewhere.

The two comment deletions and the blank-line removal in this diff are incidental
working-tree noise, not intentional changes; they are included because
reproducing the exact tree 0020 was diffed against is the whole point of the
capture.
